+ * write invalidates the page in the GPU caches, and for a page the GPU wrote (resolve
+ * readback is off, so its CPU copy is stale) that throws away the only good copy.
+ * Instead, after enough reads the page is unwatched without invalidating anything
+ * and left mapped; guest memory hashes it and checks once per frame whether the CPU
+ * changed it (Memory::SwitchUnwatchHotReadPage and SwitchCheckUnwatchedPages).
